    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d96-a2">

                <pb facs="0268" n="140" xml:id="pg140"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No.
                    410.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Consul Baiz to
                        President Bogran</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >New York</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1885-08-01"><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi> 1,
                        1885</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Sir and Friend</hi>: At this moment I have
                    learned that the house of A. D. Straus &amp; Co. has purchased the steamer City
                    of Mexico, and I am assured that it is with the object of sending her to the
                    north coast of those Republics (Central America) in response to a revolutionary
                    movement. That house is the same which a short time ago dispatched the steamer
                    Dorian with a cargo of arms and provisions for the coast of that Republic, and
                    which returned without having been able to discharge.</p>
                <p>For want of time and not having the complete details I cannot be more extended by
                    this steamer, but I will be in my next.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JACOBO BAIZ.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
